  "task_71431": {"governingAuthority": "State Property Code (Landlord-Tenant)", "regulationCode": "TX Prop. Code §§ 92.103–92.109; CA Civ. Code § 1950.5 (rules vary by state)", "plainEnglishRule": "Security deposits are resident money held by the landlord: an itemized disposition (FAS) and any refund are due within the statutory deadline after move-out (30 days in Texas, 21 in California). Deductions are allowed only for unpaid rent and damage beyond normal wear and tear.", "auditRisk": "Bad-faith retention can cost statutory damages (Texas: $100 plus three times the wrongfully withheld amount plus attorney fees; California: up to twice the deposit). Deposits must stay fully recorded as a liability.", "topic": "security_deposit"},
