  "task_97179": {"governingAuthority": "US GAAP / Loan Documents", "regulationCode": "ASC 230-10 (cash flow classification); loan cash-management / lockbox agreements; partnership agreement (distributions)", "plainEnglishRule": "Transfers between accounts and entities must follow the loan's cash-management rules (lockbox, sweep and reserve waterfalls). Owner distributions are allowed only when the loan and partnership agreements permit.", "auditRisk": "Distributions made during a lender cash-trap or covenant breach can trigger default and guarantor liability. Misclassified transfers misstate the cash flow statement.", "topic": "transfer"},
