  "task_42656": {"governingAuthority": "IRS Recordkeeping", "regulationCode": "IRC § 6001; Treas. Reg. § 1.6001-1; Rev. Proc. 98-25 (electronic records)", "plainEnglishRule": "Every transaction must be supported by source documents (invoice, contract, bank statement, calculation) kept as long as they may be material to a tax return, generally at least 3 years after filing and 7 years in practice. Electronic images are acceptable if they are complete, legible and retrievable.", "auditRisk": "Missing support lets the IRS disallow deductions (plus the 20% accuracy-related penalty under IRC § 6662), and auditors report unsupported entries as exceptions.", "topic": "attachments"},
